  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The bob of a pendulum of mass $m$, suspended by an inextensible string of length $L$ as shown in the figure carries a small charge $a$. An infinite horizontal plane conductor with uniform surface charge density $\\sigma$ is placed below it. What will be the time period of the pendulum for small amplitude oscillations?\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_q35..png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QCH4Y",
      "text": "$2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{\\left(\\mathrm{g}-\\frac{\\mathrm{mq}}{\\varepsilon_{0} \\sigma}\\right)}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6E5qE",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{\\left(\\mathrm{g}-\\frac{\\mathrm{mq} \\sigma}{\\varepsilon_{0}}\\right)}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CoV6J",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 \\pi} \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{\\left(\\mathrm{g}-\\frac{\\mathrm{q} \\sigma}{\\varepsilon_{0} \\mathrm{~m}}\\right)}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5FJz7",
      "text": "$2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{\\mathrm{L}}{\\left(\\mathrm{g}-\\frac{\\mathrm{q} \\sigma}{\\varepsilon_{0} \\mathrm{~m}}\\right)}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_phy_a35.png\">\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ Apparent weight of the bob, $w^{\\prime}=m g-q E$\r\n$$\r\nm y^{\\prime}=m g-q E\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$\r\n$g^{\\prime}=g-\\frac{q E}{m}$\r\nTime period of a pendulum. $T=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{L}{g_{e f f}}}$ $=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{L}{g-\\frac{q E}{m}}}=2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\frac{L}{\\left(g-\\frac{q \\sigma}{\\varepsilon_{0} m}\\right)}}$",
    "image": null
